From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson_hdmi: choose the colour attr on RESERVED6 under any HDR policy

atomic_check lets the driver choose the colour format and depth only in
recovery mode, under hdr_policy 1 (follow source) or a forced DV policy.
Under hdr_policy 0 (follow sink, which Kodi sets for SDR->HDR) the attr
in the connector state is carried into every mode set, so the 8-bit
YUV444/RGB a Dolby Vision tunnel needs outlives the DV session: the
desktop and the next HDR10 film go out SDR on an 8-bit link until a
reboot (hdmitx sends no HDR packet at 24-bit depth).

Kodi already asks for a fresh choice when it leaves the DV link, by
writing color_space = HDMI_COLORSPACE_RESERVED6; under follow-sink that
request reached validation as "rgb" with the old depth. Treat RESERVED6
as the explicit request it is, under any policy. Nothing else writes it,
and the other policies already choose here, so they are unchanged.

---
--- a/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
@@ -2164,8 +2164,14 @@
 	}
 
 	/*The recovery mode not have composer to set attr*/
+	/*
+	 * RESERVED6 is userspace asking the driver to choose: honour it under
+	 * any HDR policy, or a follow-sink policy carries the previous attr
+	 * (a Dolby Vision tunnel's 8-bit) into every later mode set.
+	 */
 	if ((!meson_crtc_state->uboot_mode_init && am_hdmi_info.recovery_mode) ||
-	    (get_hdr_policy() == 1) || (get_amdv_policy() == AMDV_FORCE_OUTPUT_MODE))
+	    (get_hdr_policy() == 1) || (get_amdv_policy() == AMDV_FORCE_OUTPUT_MODE) ||
+	    attr->colorformat == HDMI_COLORSPACE_RESERVED6)
 		meson_hdmitx_decide_color_attr(common, meson_crtc_state,
 						 attr, sequence_id);
 
